+# PixaCut
 
-<h1 align="center">Nuzky</h1>
+A Pixa-branded, modified edition of [Nuzky](https://github.com/nuzkyapp/nuzky), the GPL-3.0-or-later desktop editor for short-form video. Based on upstream commit `13dec1d70da91b5506ccceec3e05b275de708314`. Version 0.1.10-alpha.
 
-<p align="center">
-  A free, open-source video editor for your computer, in the spirit of CapCut.<br>
-  <a href="https://nuzky.app">nuzky.app</a> · <a href="#install">Download</a> · <a href="#build-and-run">Build it</a> · <a href="CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribute</a>
-</p>
+## Current status
 
-<img src="assets/readme/editor.webp" width="100%" alt="The Nuzky editor as drawn on nuzky.app: imported clips on the left, a vertical video with a caption in the middle, the clip's settings on the right and captions, clips and music on the timeline below">
-<p align="center"><sub>The editor as drawn on nuzky.app. The alpha differs in places.</sub></p>
+Private local rebranding prototype. Frontend lint, TypeScript and production frontend build pass. Native editor/runtime acceptance, installers, own updater keys/feed, Pixa suite account integration, Mac signing/notarization and public release are not complete. No public PixaCut repository, website listing or installer has been published.
 
-Cut a talking video by deleting words from its transcript, caption it with speech recognition that runs on your own machine, and let an AI agent do the tedious parts while you watch. Nuzky is licensed under GPLv3 and has a native Rust engine.
+The editor retains the upstream timeline, local Whisper captions, audio tools, effects, AI-agent integration, guided tour and project workflows. Upstream is alpha: this fork is not claimed to match CapCut feature-for-feature.
 
-**Nuzky is in alpha.** It is early, so expect rough edges. Nuzky never changes or deletes your original videos.
